Login sessions
==============

Needs core's session.sql (uniliquid/core, README "Session additions")
applied to the database BEFORE this frontend is deployed: without the
column session.logged_in_at every visitor with a session cookie gets the
error page ('column "logged_in_at" does not exist').

Needs uniliquid/webmcp with the set_cookie arguments max_age, http_only
and same_site. An older WebMCP silently ignores them: sessions work, but
the cookie has no Max-Age (a login ends with the browser), HttpOnly or
SameSite. The deployment's check of the cookie headers catches this.

- Anonymous session: created on the first request without a valid cookie,
  24 hours from then (core's column default); browser-session cookie.
- Login and registration: a new session (new ident and CSRF secret), the
  anonymous one is deleted (no session fixation); the language is kept.
  It expires config.session_idle_lifetime (default 30 days) after the last
  renewal, never later than config.session_max_lifetime (default 90 days)
  after the login. The expiry is renewed at most once per
  config.session_renew_interval (default 1 hour). The cookie has Max-Age,
  so a login survives closing the browser; use "Logout" on shared
  computers.
- Cookie liquid_feedback_session: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, secure with an
  https base URL.
- Logout: the session is deleted and replaced by a new anonymous one.
- Password change: logged out on all other devices, a new session on the
  current one. Password reset and admin "deactivate": logged out on all
  devices. Lock (any way): core's trigger deletes the sessions.
- An expired session is not used, even before lf_update deletes it.
- Sessions without logged_in_at (logged in before this code) are not
  extended; they end at their stored expiry.

The settings are "<number> minute(s)|hour(s)|day(s)" (PostgreSQL
intervals, config/example.lua), with renew interval < idle lifetime <=
maximum lifetime; config/init.lua stops with "Invalid configuration: ..."
otherwise. A change takes effect on new logins and renewals; stored
expiries are not shortened.

A member locked while logging in gets no session (Session:login reads the
member row FOR SHARE and only for an unlocked member).

Tests (Docker): tests/run.sh
